{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548015-uratha-and-the-safety-of-consuming-chocolate","id":1548015,"title":"Uratha and the Safety of Consuming Chocolate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-28T22:48:40-08:00","id":1548015,"title":"Uratha and the Safety of Consuming Chocolate","content":"A more light-hearted subject, especially for Uratha with a sweet tooth before their First Change.<br /> <br /> Chocolate is toxic to Canines.<br /> <br /> Uratha are Canines.<br /> <br /> Would it therefore be dangerous for them to eat chocolate as humans then transform into their canine forms before it is fully digested, I wonder? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T04:43:06-08:00","id":1548022,"title":"","content":"Uratha aren't canines. Unlike the Garou (since you put a post in each of these) all Uratha start as humans with the spiritual aspects of a wolf as part of their being that gets activated fully at some point in life.<br /> <br /> Also, theobromine, the chemical that's so dangerous to dogs, is actually toxic to pretty much every mammal, dogs are just worse at processing it than most. There's nothing &quot;special&quot; where theobromine does something different to dogs than humans. A big part of it is that dogs generally weigh less than humans (and wolves for that matter) so they get sick from quantities of chocolate that don't register to most humans. A dog needs to eat about 5 ounces of milk chocolate per kilogram of weight to get into serious medical intervention levels of theobromine toxicity. Below that they're going to be sick, but like a hang over there's not much to do besides wait for the toxins to flush out and keep hydrated. A lot of the worry about dogs and chocolate is that most pets are toy or small dogs, which are utterly tiny compared to a wolf and hit the dangerous zone far faster for it.<br /> <br /> Even if you considered Uratha to be susceptible to theobromine toxicity from eating food in Hishu and then turning into a wolf, a 4 oz milk chocolate bar (a fairly large single serving of chocolate), is probably not enough to make a wolf noticeable sick considering their body mass.<br /> <br /> When you take into account things like how supernaturally hardy the Uratha are... it's just not a concern unless a character is literally gorging themselves on pounds of chocolate (or eating more concentrated forms of chocolate like dark baker's chocolate which... doesn't taste very good and still would require a lot of it). <br /> <br /> Basically, it doesn't matter one way or the other. Unless you have a pack of Uratha that decide to also be trying to become stars of a show like Jackass but for werewolves, where they down lots and lots of chocolate just to see how sick they can make themselves before having to change out of their wolf forms, eating that much chocolate just isn't going to happen to any werewolf not looking to tempt fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T14:29:19-08:00","id":1548035,"title":"","content":"1e also addresses chocolate and caffeine in Blood of the Wolf's section on how drugs interact with werewolf physiology (pages 23-27), for what it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T19:22:40-08:00","id":1548041,"title":"","content":"Considering that Second Edition gives them a spiritually driven physiology where they can't even survive on anything other than meat past a certain Primal Urge, I think there might be a case for something like chocolate just not registering in their digestion one way or the other above a certain point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T00:39:18-08:00","id":1548045,"title":"","content":"Considering the books don't include immunity to ingested toxins and poisons stemming from that, I doubt that was the intent. I remember when that came out, we had a few debates about what that meant for Uratha that ate non-meat food items, and the dev/authors at the time were largely of the &quot;this is spirit magic, stop overthinking it,&quot; position. IIRC the basic take away was that Uratha of high Primal Urge that eat a salad would, under scientific scrutiny, appear to be digesting it like a normal human, but their growing spiritual power just blocks their bodies from actually deriving any value from it; not something like they have to avoid non-meat items or face having to expel the non-meat out one hole or the other... rapidly.. due to their bodies flat out rejecting it.<br /> <br /> Of course, the higher the PU, the greater the Uratha's base-line regeneration, and the less of a threat the same amount of chocolate would be anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T02:16:53-08:00","id":1548048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1548015-uratha-and-the-safety-of-consuming-chocolate?p=1548045#post1548045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the books don't include immunity to ingested toxins and poisons stemming from that, I doubt that was the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not everything needs to be intended to be able to make a case for it, but fair enough regardless.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T02:53:16-08:00","id":1548050,"title":"","content":"Still a fair point of your own. I wouldn't really care about authorial intent if a player tried to abuse the way the Drug/Poison rules and the Uratha regeneration rules work to attack a werewolf right as the next Toxicity interval hits to try to do enough damage to roll over into Agg. Toxins don't actually hit you in regular waves of X damage every hour on the hour. And while it's useful to know that a PU 3 Uratha heals 8L an hour, which is more than the most severe OD of normal drugs can do (Toxicity 7 is listed as the highest of mundane drug overdoses) in the same period of time, to know that the Uratha basically don't die from doing lots of drugs; I think most people would prefer to see that as something that happens in-character consistently over time, not in the solid intervals the mechanics use for pacing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}